{
 "id": "det-pe-morphisms-etale-comparison",
 "blueprint": {
  "is": "det-pe-morphisms-etale-comparison",
  "from": null,
  "same_as": null
 },
 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Étale, affine pro-étale and weakly étale morphisms",
 "statement": "Let $u\\colon U\\to X$ be a morphism of schemes.\n\n1. If $u$ is étale, then $u$ is weakly étale [def-weil-weakly-etale-morphism].\n2. If $X=\\operatorname{Spec}R$ and $u$ is affine pro-étale, i.e. $U=\\operatorname{Spec}B$\n   with $R\\to B$ ind-étale [def-weil-pbc-ind-etale-algebra], then $u$ is weakly étale.\n3. If $u$ is weakly étale and locally of finite presentation, then $u$ is étale.\n4. On affine charts $U\\supset\\operatorname{Spec}B\\to\\operatorname{Spec}R\\subset X$, $u$ is\n   weakly étale if and only if $R\\to B$ and the multiplication $B\\otimes_RB\\to B$ are flat.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/main-20261015/blueprint/sec-proetale-coefficients/sk-def-pe-morphisms/det-pe-morphisms-etale-comparison.md",
  "place": "node det-pe-morphisms-etale-comparison, order None"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [
  "def-weil-weakly-etale-morphism",
  "def-weil-pbc-ind-etale-algebra"
 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "*4.* Flatness is local on source and target. The diagonal $\\Delta_u$ maps the affine open\n$\\operatorname{Spec}B$ into the affine open\n$\\operatorname{Spec}B\\times_{\\operatorname{Spec}R}\\operatorname{Spec}B=\\operatorname{Spec}(B\\otimes_RB)$,\nwhere it is the closed immersion given by multiplication $B\\otimes_RB\\to B$; such opens\ncover the source of $\\Delta_u$ and their images lie in opens of this form covering a\nneighbourhood of $\\Delta_u(U)$. Hence $u$ and $\\Delta_u$ are flat if and only if all the\nchart maps $R\\to B$ and $B\\otimes_RB\\to B$ are flat.",
   "uses": [],
   "elementary": null
  },
  {
   "text": "*1.* An étale morphism is flat. It is also unramified and locally of finite presentation,\nso its diagonal is an open immersion (Stacks Project, Morphisms, unramified morphisms), and open immersions are flat.",
   "uses": [],
   "elementary": null
  },
  {
   "text": "*2.* An ind-étale ring map is weakly étale by [lem-weil-pbc-ind-etale-stability]: $B$ is\nflat over $R$ as a filtered colimit of flat algebras, and $B\\otimes_RB\\to B$ is\nind-Zariski, hence flat. Apply 4.",
   "uses": [
    "lem-weil-pbc-ind-etale-stability"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  },
  {
   "text": "*3.* Let $u$ be weakly étale and locally of finite presentation. The diagonal of a\nmorphism locally of finite presentation is locally of finite presentation (Stacks Project, Morphisms, morphisms locally of finite presentation). The diagonal is a monomorphism, and it is flat by assumption. A flat monomorphism\nlocally of finite presentation is an open immersion (Stacks Project, Étale morphisms of schemes). So $\\Delta_u$ is\nan open immersion, i.e. $u$ is unramified (Stacks Project, Morphisms, unramified morphisms). A flat, unramified morphism\nlocally of finite presentation is étale.",
   "uses": [],
   "elementary": null
  }
 ],
 "proof_deps": [
  "lem-weil-pbc-ind-etale-stability"
 ],
